# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Environments
.venv/
env/
venv/
ENV/

# Testing & Coverage
.coverage
.coverage.*
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
tmp/

# Argus Engine Output & Cache
.argus/
_bmad-output/reports/

# Build artifacts (Story 9.2 — the release workflow builds these into ./dist and the
# GitHub Release is where they are published; they are never committed).
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# IDE / Tooling
.agent/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
coverage.xml

# Per-run audit output (added 2026-08-19). These are REGENERATED by running the tool
# and carry run-scoped ids, timestamps and at least one absolute host path
# (.bmad-drift-audit/audit-20260810-0839/audit-report.md), so committing them would
# put machine-specific bytes in the record and invite a stale run being read as current.
#
# NOTE the trailing `*/`: `_bmad-output/audit-reports/coverage-ledger.md` and
# `final-verdict.md` are TRACKED and stay tracked — only the per-run SUBDIRECTORIES
# (self-audit/, run-demo/, ollama-audit/) are ignored. A blanket
# `_bmad-output/audit-reports/` would read as ignoring those two as well, which is
# false and would mislead the next reader.
.bmad-drift-audit/
_bmad-output/audit-reports/*/

# ⚠️ AUTHORED, NOT GENERATED — ignored on operator instruction 2026-08-19, flagged here
# because that is a judgement call worth being able to reverse in one line. Neither is
# tool output: `bmad-dev-loop-pack/` is the SM/Dev/Review/Retro subagent pack plus its
# two installers and SKILL.md, and `argusdemo/demo.sh` is a hand-written demo. Ignoring
# them means they are never version-controlled and are lost with the working tree.
# Delete these two lines to track them.
argusdemo/
bmad-dev-loop-pack/

# ⚠️ REGENERATED BY-PRODUCT, ignored 2026-08-29 — and the reason is a claim this repository
# has already published. `sprint-change-proposal-2026-08-10.md` records as MEASURED FACT that
# there is "No MSIX, PyInstaller, Briefcase, Nuitka, cx_Freeze, `.spec` or `.iss` anywhere in
# the tree". Committing `argus.spec` would falsify that line, and no guard would catch it.
#
# It is also load-bearing for nothing: `.github/workflows/build-binaries.yml` invokes
# `pyinstaller --onefile --name argus …` with CLI flags and never reads a spec file. The file
# appears when someone runs that command by hand — PyInstaller writes one as a side effect.
# Delete this line if a spec file ever becomes the real build input; then correct the proposal.
argus.spec

# Session scratch — working notes and one-off scripts, never part of the record.
scratch/
